BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annie
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261228
DTSTAMP:20261111T182120Z
UID:ed2616def2bfcf8b4712bcac14c6@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Leapin' Lizards! The musical that stole America’s heart come
 s home to celebrate its 50th anniversary on the stage where it all began! 
 With pluck and positivity\, Annie escapes Miss Hannigan’s orphanage in s
 earch of her parents and finds a new family with her lovable mutt Sandy an
 d billionaire Oliver Warbucks. This dazzling new production bursts with jo
 y and timeless songs like “Tomorrow\,” “It’s the Hard Knock Life\,
 ” and “Maybe.” You can bet your bottom dollar—it’s the can’t-m
 iss event of the season!\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/annie
LOCATION:The Goodspeed\, 6 Main Street\, East Haddam CT\, 06423
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/annie
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Hepburn Women: A Special Exhibit
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270130
DTSTAMP:20261111T182120Z
UID:02edc57db2d9a2dc623955b50c6a@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Katharine Hepburn was not an island\, but was one in a line of
  unique and powerful women. In this exhibit\, we widen the spotlight to en
 compass three generations of extraordinary Hepburns: Mrs. Katharine “Kit
 ” Houghton Hepburn\; Katharine\, Marion\, and Margaret Hepburn\; and Kat
 harine Houghton. Each one\, shaped by the generations before and after her
 \, lived out loud and left an impact in her wake. Mothers\, sisters\, acti
 vists\, librarians\, actors—these are The Hepburn Women. On display thro
 ugh early 2027 (closing date TBD)\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/he
 pburn-women-special-exhibit
LOCATION:Katharine Hepburn Cultural Arts Center\, 300 Main Street\, Old Sa
 ybrook CT\, 06475
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/hepburn-women-special-exhibit
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
